 "notes": "Curve digitised from Fig. 5 (solid black MICROSCOPE line) of the e-print raster fig_de.png via pixel tracing with axis calibration (frame x: 1e-24..1e-10 eV, y: 1e-9..1). This is the constraint on |d_e| for a dilaton coupled only to the electromagnetic sector, obtained from the D_mtilde=0 subspace with D_e = 0.00027 d_e^2, derived from MICROSCOPE's 2-sigma Eotvos-parameter measurement. Paper convention Delta(alpha_EM)/alpha_EM = d_e phi/M_P with M_P^-1 = sqrt(4 pi G), identical to the Damour-Donoghue kappa convention, so no conversion applied. Limit is flat at |d_e| ~ 2.3e-4 below ~1e-13 eV (curve shown from 1e-24 eV, left edge of the figure) and rises steeply, leaving the plot (d_e~1) near 2.2e-11 eV. WEP test, no dark-matter density assumption. The paper also gives Yukawa |alpha|(lambda) limits for q=B and q=B-L (Figs 1-2) and dilaton (D_mtilde, D_e) constraints (Figs 3-4); the d_e limit is the one directly in a canonical plane.",
